
📋 AI Fairness Compliance Report (NIST AI RMF v1.0)Project Name: Recruitment-AI Bias AuditVersion: 1.0 (Audit Date: Feb 2026)Lead Auditor: Venkatesan Ramanathan (Venky)System Classification: High-Risk (Employment) - EU AI Act Annex III1. Executive Summary 📑A technical audit was conducted on the automated screening system using the Fairlearn toolkit. The initial assessment identified a Critical Finding regarding gender-based performance disparity. Following the identification, a Mitigation Strategy (Exponentiated Gradient) was applied to align the system with the 80% (4/5ths) legal threshold for fairness.2. NIST Function: MEASURE (Technical Findings) 📏We evaluated the model's Selection Rate (Demographic Parity) across Gender groups.MetricPre-Mitigation (Baseline)Post-Mitigation (Mitigated)Male Selection Rate25.19%15.20%Female Selection Rate7.17%14.10%Disparity Ratio0.28 (FAIL)0.93 (PASS)Audit Note: The baseline ratio of 0.28 indicates that the model was 3.5x more likely to select male candidates, representing a high risk of "Direct Discrimination" under US and EU law.3. NIST Function: MAP (Context & Risks) 🗺️Intended Use: Automated resume screening for mid-to-high level professional roles.Sociotechnical Risk: Historical hiring data contained systemic gender bias. Left unmanaged, the AI would have amplified this bias, leading to legal liability and loss of diverse talent.Regulatory Impact: Failure to address this would violate EEOC guidelines (US) and the EU AI Act (Global).4. NIST Function: MANAGE (Remediation Actions) 🛠️To resolve the identified risk, the following technical controls were implemented:In-Processing Mitigation: Utilized the ExponentiatedGradient algorithm to enforce fairness constraints during the training phase.Trade-off Analysis: While the fairness ratio improved from 0.28 to 0.93, a marginal 2% decrease in overall model accuracy was accepted to ensure legal compliance.Human-in-the-Loop: A policy was established requiring human review for any high-confidence candidate rejected by the model during the pilot phase.5. Auditor Certification 📜This system is now rated as COMPLIANT with basic algorithmic fairness standards (4/5ths Rule).

